"An auriad is a loop of iridescent white string that bonds to its owner's authority."
"Once bonded it belongs to its owner alone and turns their favorite color."
"Bonding takes days; afterward it feels sticky, like a third hand."
"It is as strong as its owner's authority; only hot fire or a powerful knife could break it."
"Spells are cast by making string shapes and touching the gaps with authority."
"It grows stronger with use and passively bolsters its owner's authority."
"Wizards wear them as bracelets, necklaces or hair ties; touching another's uncalled is rude."
"Wizards who dislike hand casting have theirs severed after school."
"A Year Six graduation auriad spell throws a square hammer of force about thirty yards."
